# Good Upstream Contributor Policy (GUCP)

Read [`docs/good-upstream-contributor-policy.md`](../../docs/good-upstream-contributor-policy.md) for the registry. Skill: [`.cursor/skills/envyos-good-upstream-contributor/SKILL.md`](../skills/envyos-good-upstream-contributor/SKILL.md).

## On every envycore / bootloader / motatool commit batch

1. **Triage** — split the batch into logical upstream units; classify each (see skill table).
2. **Register** — add or update rows in `docs/good-upstream-contributor-policy.md` in the **same session** (target release section when CHANGELOG `[Unreleased]` names that distro; else § Unreleased).
3. **Flag** — status **`candidate`** is correct at commit time. Do not defer registration to release prep.
4. **Audit** — run `./envyos gucp audit` when unsure anything was missed.

While a PR is open, sync commits per [upstream-pr-sync.mdc](upstream-pr-sync.mdc).

## Before distro finalize (release prep)

1. Run `./envyos gucp audit vX.Y.Z` — handle every **`candidate`** / **`extracting`** row.
2. Extract pure `feature/<name>` branches and open cross-fork PRs → status **`submitted`**.
3. Promote registry rows to **`## Release vX.Y.Z`**; mirror **`### Upstream PRs`** in CHANGELOG.
4. Run **`./envyos gucp check vX.Y.Z`** — must pass.
5. **`./envyos publish finalize`** also enforces the gate.

**Release is incomplete** until every upstreamable row for that version is **`submitted`** or **`merged`**. `candidate` and `extracting` block finalize.
